    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this dashboard can and cannot see",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 63
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Quota is the vendor's own number** for Z.ai (both Coding Plan pools), **Claude Pro** and **ChatGPT Plus / Codex** (5-hour and 7-day utilisation, the same endpoints their own CLIs read), **OpenCode Go** (5-hour, weekly and monthly percent of the subscription, from `inference/go/v1/usage` with opencode's console login; its lanes use only the free models), and DeepSeek and Moonshot (dollar balances). Polled every 15 minutes by a background refresher and served from cache; a reading older than 3 hours is ignored for routing.\n\n**MiMo's balance is derived, not published.** Xiaomi offers no balance endpoint, so the figure is an operator-recorded console reading less everything opencode has booked against the provider since. Re-anchor after a top-up.\n\n**SuperGrok's figure costs a request.** xAI publishes no quota endpoint; the plan's headroom arrives as `x-ratelimit-{limit,remaining}-{tokens,requests}` on a chat response \u2014 the same numbers the CLI's `/usage` screen shows. The exporter reads it with a one-token completion, so it refreshes hourly rather than every 15 minutes.\n\n**Cash is real; notional is modelled.** Prepaid tiers cost nothing at the margin, so *Avoided by prepaid* prices their tokens at the cheapest metered equivalent's list price. An estimate, not an invoice.\n\n**Token counts are normalised per harness** \u2014 codex reports input inclusive of its cached prefix while opencode and grok report cache separately. Raw fields differ by roughly an order of magnitude and must not be compared directly."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "bargauge",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 51
      },
      "title": "Metered spend to date \u2014 including MiMo",
      "description": "Cumulative cash per metered plan. MiMo is purely pay-as-you-go and is charged like DeepSeek and Kimi; it is here rather than in the balances panel only because Xiaomi publishes no balance endpoint to read.",
      "targets": [
